<title>SINGAPORE: Smooth Hong Kong handover 70 pct likely - Templeton.</title>
<headline>Smooth Hong Kong handover 70 pct likely - Templeton.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A smooth handover of power in Hong Kong with little disruption to its financial markets is 70 percent probable, fund managers Templeton Investment Management said on Friday.</p>
<p>Mark Mobius, managing director of Hong Kong-based Templeton, told a business conference there was a chance of Beijing becoming actively involved after the territory reverts to Chinese soveriegnty at the end of June.</p>
<p>He said it was possible China could decree tax rises and impose restrictions on Hong Kong that could damage its economy, but suggested that was unlikely.</p>
</text>
